WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.960
Lord Gwyn's Firstborn son was a God of War

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.520
Who inherited the sunlight from his father

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.480
The power of Sunlight is manifest as lightning

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.660
And it's highly effective against dragons

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.760
And Gwyn's Firstborn son was once a Dragonslayer

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.740
who fought against his father's ancient enemy

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.260
And as you know, the ancient dragons once ruled

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:31.480
over an Age of Grey

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.040
but Gwyn discovered their weakness and he struck them down

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.660
with Great Bolts of Lightning

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.200
Later, advancements in arms would lead to lightning imbued spears

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.420
with a cross-pummel

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.500
which were developped to be stamped or thrust

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.480
deep into the flesh of dragons

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.460
The Firstborn's Dragonslayer Swordspear

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.360
was the first of such weapons

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.220
for the Firstborn had respect only for arms and nothing else

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.520
At some point, during the war, however

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.060
Gwyn's Firstborn had a change of heart

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.480
He switched sides, and

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:10.080
sacrificed everything to ally himself with the ancient dragons

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.760
And, unlike a lot of Souls lore,

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.800
this part of history is actually described as

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.440
''missing'' for a reason:

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:21.620
for, after he sided with the ancient dragons,

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:24.360
Lord Gwyn's Firstborn was expunged

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.900
from the annals of history

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.760
and his deific status

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:28.800
was recinded.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.720
He was no longer considered a God,

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.860
no longer in the books of history and,

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.720
today, even his name is not known

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.600
If you played it around the time that Dark Souls 1 was released,

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.420
the identity of the Firstborn

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:45.920
was a complete mystery to all of us.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.000
All we knew was that he was Gwyn's Firstborn,

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.440
that he was a God of War,

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:53.640
and that he was a core part of the Warrior's of Sunlight,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.200
so players puzzled over

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.000
missing statues next to Gwyn;

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.080
they puzzled over

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.640
broken monuments to the Warriors of Sunlight,

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.180
and

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:02.440
we even guessed

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.120
that the Firstborn himself

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.520
could have just been a simple man

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.120
from Astora who fought for the Sun

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.340
and, it is true that

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.320
the God of War continued to watch

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:13.840
over his Sunlight Warriors,

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.000
but we can now finally

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.000
see where he went,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.900
and why.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.340
The Nameless King,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.080
the Firstborn Son of Gwyn,

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.360
Heir of Sunlight,

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.640
and God of War

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.620
left the miracle, Sunlight Blade,

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.480
upon his father's coffin,

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.660
perhaps as a final farewell.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.360
Now, this part of

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.860
the Nameless King's history,

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.420
it's been purposefully

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.100
erased,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.340
but some players

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.140
do think

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.160
that traces of his existence

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.120
still remain

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.220
out in the world

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.400
and cannot be erased.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.160
In fact,

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.820
it's a popular theory,

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:48.780
and I'll leave a link

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.600
to a few sources

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.400
in the description,

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.080
that

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.460
the Namless King

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.220
is referenced

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.460
in the Faraam Armor Set,

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.020
which is this plate set

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:57.980
that was named

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:59.760
after a God of War.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.360
The mighty Lion Knights of Forossa

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.080
were worshippers of the War God, Faraam,

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.320
wore heavy armor,

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:09.440
and were feared for their two-handed swordplay.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.080
This armor was blessed

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.680
by the War God, Faraam.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.120
Forossa would later fall

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.560
to conflict with their neighbors,

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.000
and the legacy of the Faraam Knights

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:19.800
fell with it.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.080
So, the information

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.280
here is also lacking,

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.040
but is the Nameless King

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.540
the War God Faraam?

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.260
Well, that's up to you to decide.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.340
Both are described as War Gods;

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.020
both place high value

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.140
in arms.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.540
The Nameless King had to be

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.360
king of some realm, and

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.080
the Faraam Set is blessed

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.980
and named after a God of War,

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.480
who is possibly

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:45.780
the one emblazed upon the helm

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:46.760
as a knight

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.000
facing a dragon.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.540
Also, both the Nameless King

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.860
and the Kingdom of Forossa

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.400
fell from power,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.140
so, hey, whatever you believe.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:58.440
This is a classic example of Souls

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.940
leaving just enough clues

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.480
that you can choose to believe

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.240
or not choose to believe,

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.720
so no one is provably right or wrong.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.940
But moving on to what we do know

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.480
The Nameless King

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:11.840
tamed a Storm Drake

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.700
upon which he lead a lifetime of battle.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.960
Assumedly, this partnership with the Storm Drake

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.680
was a part of the Firstborn

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:22.120
allying with the Acient Dragons.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:23.320
I have a few suspicions

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.980
that the Storm Drake might also

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.480
be known as a giant horned oni,

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.720
which are found in eastern lands

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.720
as the Onislayer Greatarrow describes,

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:35.000
and it's the only creature in the game

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.940
that really fits the description

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.100
of an Oni,

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.580
whatever creature that is,

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:40.860
and it's certainly

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:41.700
a drake that looks

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.020
very much like a foreign

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:44.660
offshoot of most other

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.600
draconic creatures in Souls.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.700
It looks nothing like them really.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.060
Oni are also found

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.420
in an eastern land,

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.700
and Forossa is in an eastern land as well, so

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.040
maybe there's something here,

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:57.760
but just speculation.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.100
When the Storm Drake fell,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.920
the King claimed its soul,

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.360
as was customary

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.920
in the Age of the Gods.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.320
In a giant flash,

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.500
we see the Nameless King become imbued

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.780
with the drake's power of the Storm,

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:13.280
which is really reminiscent of

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:14.640
Ornstein and Smough

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.900
absorbing one another in their boss fight

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.400
in Dark Souls I

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.780
as the Age of the Gods was drawing to a close there.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.080
Dark Souls III's description of Smough's Great Hammer

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.620
tells us that Smough

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:29.220
was the last knight to remain at his post,

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.320
guarding the ruined cathedral.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.400
Ornstein, on the other hand,

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.300
he long guarded the ruined cathedral,

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.780
but he left the land in search

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.200
of the Nameless King.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.740
So, you're probably asking yourself,

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.400
"How did Ornstein leave the cathedral

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.640
if I killed him in Dark Souls I,

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:49.040
and then again in Dark Souls II?".

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:50.560
Well, remember

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:53.240
Dark Souls III is the game that

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.240
very openly references the fact

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.880
that events are doomed to repeat themselves.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.960
More than any previous game,

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.080
this is a game about cycles

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.660
and the Lords of Cinder who contributed

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:06.040
to their own cycle.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.020
We see so many cycles

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.620
laid before us, so,

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:11.420
yes, a lot of narratives

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:12.900
and plots in the game

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.360
have been recycled.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.200
In a way, that's what the games are about,

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:16.760
but

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:17.980
in Dark Souls III,

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.500
it's nice because a lot of these plots

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.920
are further along than ever before

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.980
Take Ornstein, for example,

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.160
in this timeline, he survived

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:30.520
until he tired of standing around in the cathedral,

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:31.880
and he left,

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:35.080
for during this dragonless age

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.680
where he stood in the cathedral,

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.480
Ornstein the Dragonslayer

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.220
must have felt quite bereft of purpose,

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:44.600
so he left in search of the Nameless King.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:46.620
So the question becomes,

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.640
"Did he intend to kill the Nameless King

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:51.780
or did he intend to serve him?".

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.520
Ornstein's Set in Dark Souls I

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:56.480
describes Ornstein as

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:59.340
the captain of the four knights of Lord Gwyn,

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.800
but the Leo Ring of Dark Souls III

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:03.800
describes him as the first knight

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.800
of the sun's eldest born,

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.280
the Nameless King.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.060
So, since I found it hard to believe

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:11.220
that he could be both

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:13.400
the captain of the guard to Gwyn,

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:17.640
and simultaneously the first knight of the Firstborn.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:19.160
I think it's most likely that

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.760
Ornstein abandoned his duty as captain of the guard,

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:26.760
and then decided to serve the Nameless King instead

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.640
after he was exiled.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:30.220
But, the best evidence

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.080
that Ornstein remained a friend

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:33.520
to the Nameless King

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.860
is the Sacred Oath description, which

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:37.880
labels him as not just

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:40.200
the Nameless King's first knight,

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:43.200
but his faithful first knight.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.800
Since the game is clarifying something like this,

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.860
then I am going to believe that

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.960
he is loyal to the Nameless King.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:52.200
So, Ornstein tracks down

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.280
and pledges alleigance to the Nameless King,

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.100
but what becomes of Ornstein

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.380
after his arrival in Archdragon peak?

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:01.980
We find his armor and his weapon

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.240
after the Nameless King fight,

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.240
but it's just discarded to the side;

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:07.960
it's not upon a corpse;

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.560
it's not in a chest,

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:11.100
and this is strange

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.440
for Souls, right?

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:13.640
It stands out.

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:15.980
I don't think there's many examples of this happening.

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:17.980
Uh so, sure, it wouldn't make sense

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:19.860
for the armor to be upon a corpse,

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:24.260
but items like this are, at least, meant to be in chests.

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.720
So, to me,

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:27.540
it signifies that Ornstein

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:31.220
didn't want to preserve anything at all from his past

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:32.660
or, perhaps that

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:34.280
he discarded his armor

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.200
in the same way that many people here do

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:40.220
to begin the transformation into a dragon.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:42.300
So, is Ornstein alive?

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.340
is he dead?

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:45.240
Was he killed by the Nameless King?

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:48.440
Or did he become one of the Dragons in the shrine?

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.160
His fate is left open

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.800
for you to decide.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.000
So, we've mentioned

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.940
the spell, Sacred Oath, before

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:56.780
and its description reads

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:57.820
"Sacred Oath,

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:00.780
miracle devised by Warriors of the Sun

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:03.520
tells the tale of the Sun's Firstborn,

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.660
his faithful first knight,

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:09.440
and the brave dragonslayer who served them both.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:12.380
The brave dragonslayer who served them both

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:13.560
So a few

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:15.880
dragonslayers could fit this description,

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.720
but I think it's most likely

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.380
that this was Havel.

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:20.820
Havel the Rock

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:22.900
was a battlefield compatriot of Gwyn,

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:23.980
the First Lord.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.980
He was suited in this armor

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.700
carved from solid rock

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.720
and he wields the tooth of an Everlasting Dragon

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.120
Havel was followed

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.580
by warriors who replicated

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:35.720
his armaments, his weaponry, and

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:38.620
never flinched nor retreated from battle

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:42.600
Havel was the arch enemy of Seath the Scaless,

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.900
which was the dragon who betrayed his own

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:46.940
and allied with Lord Gwyn

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:47.840
This

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:50.360
must have placed Havel in an awkward spot.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:52.460
He's a battlefield compatriot

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:53.560
of Lord Gwyn

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:54.320
and yet,

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:56.860
Gwyn allied with a magic wielding

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:58.320
traitorous dragon

00:09:58.320 --> 00:09:59.500
that Havel hates

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:00.760
In Dark Souls I,

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:01.840
it's implied

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:04.400
that Havel was locked away by a dear friend

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:04.900
and

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:06.940
all that time ago we theorized

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:08.340
that it was Gwyn himself

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:10.660
who locked his Hollowed friend away.

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:11.800
We also talked about

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:13.980
how a piece of occult weaponry was

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:15.800
capable of killing the Gods

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.020
and it was locked

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.260
away in a basement

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:20.380
with the rest of Havel's gear,

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:22.200
and this fueled some theory

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.600
that Havel plotted against the Gods

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.000
In Lordran,

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.180
Havel remained locked in that basement,

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:28.680
but,

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:30.060
in Dark Souls III,

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:33.460
perhaps, we see a different path to Havel's tale

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:35.100
We find armaments left

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:36.340
by Havel himself

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:37.780
in Archdragon Peak,

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.700
and we can easily theorize that

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:42.360
Havel was the dragonslayer mentioned

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.280
in the tale of Sacred Oath

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.620
A brave dragonslayer,

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.100
the keyword being brave,

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:50.980
who never flinched nor retreated from battle,

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:51.480
and

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:52.640
had good cause

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.920
to take up arms with the Nameless King,

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:56.380
who was another leader

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:58.640
positioned to rebel gainst Gwyn

00:10:58.760 --> 00:10:59.260
and

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:01.040
Seath the Scaless

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:02.100
Of course,

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:03.440
to play devil's advocate,

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:04.940
Havel could also be there

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:06.920
to slay the Nameless King.

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:08.420
He is overlooking the corpse

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:09.700
of an Ancient Dragon

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:10.680
after all.

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:11.180
But,

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:13.060
as a final piece of proof

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:15.440
that he's on the Nameless King's side

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.280
The half-dragon summoners,

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:19.040
the ones with the frilly necks

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:21.560
that summon phantoms to fight against you,

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.820
they summon Warriors of Havel

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:24.720
to fight.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:26.280
Also, I want to point out

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:27.020
that they summon

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:28.620
a half-naked dude

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.420
wielding Ricard's Rapier

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:31.860
and wearing a crown,

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.280
so I'm assuming this is Ricard as well,

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:36.280
and it links Prince Ricard

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:37.440
to a king;

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:39.680
it links him to the Way of the Dragon,

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:41.620
and it links him to

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:42.920
yet another castle

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:46.100
full of half-dragon snake creatures.

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:46.880
So,

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:49.040
that is pretty much everything surrounding

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:50.080
the Nameless King

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:50.980
explained.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:52.180
So, what do you believe?

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:54.500
The story is really open-ended

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:56.400
and I've given you most of the

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.220
raw information you need

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:00.000
to tell your own story.

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:01.740
But regardless, now you know

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.400
the story of Archdragon Peak

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:05.620
where the Son of Gwyn switched sides,

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.900
separated himself from the fire linking fiasco,

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:10.320
and assumedly,

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:12.920
quitely began rebuilding the ranks

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.440
of the Ancient Dragons.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:16.500
So we just talked about

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.400
how Havel hated the dragon

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.440
named Seath the Scaleless,

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:22.760
a traitorous, mad pale drake

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.120
whose twisted soul

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:24.700
clearly

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:27.160
lives on in Oceiros, the Consumed king.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:30.280
Oceiros was once king of Lothric,

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:32.440
married to a queen who was revered

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:35.260
as a goddess of fertility and bounty,

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:36.240
much like

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.480
Gwynevere from Dark Souls I, and

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:40.800
as we know from the previous video

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.900
The Lothric line was obsessed

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:45.020
with creating a worthy heir

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:47.640
and the rite of the linking of the Fire

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:49.940
Oceiros, however,

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:51.320
in his later years,

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:53.820
became fascinated with dragons.

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:55.520
His research lead him

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:56.400
to the heretics

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:58.660
of the Grand Archives of Lothric,

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.200
where he discovered

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:03.280
the twisted worship of Seath, the Pale Drake.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:04.920
Eventually, he discovered

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:07.220
the research that was done by Big Hat Logan,

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.280
who you'll remember from Dark Souls I.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:11.200
He was this legendary scholar

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.200
who went mad

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.560
delving into Seath's sorceries.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:17.120
So Oceiros was inspired,

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:19.680
he was edified by Big Hat Logan

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:20.220
and

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:21.280
he even learned

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.420
how to perform the Crystal Breath

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:25.380
of Seath the Scaleless.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:26.980
He was transforming into

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:27.860
this dragon.

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:29.060
He was changing

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:29.620
and

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.000
behind Oceiros,

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.580
we see the rest of his chambers,

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:35.100
and they're full of dragon scales and

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:36.780
dead man servants, and

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:38.380
there's even a Drakeblood Knight

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.880
in the Way of the Dragon pose.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.720
Oceiros himself was

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:46.300
clearly somewhat successful at

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.720
turning into an Ancient Dragon, and

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.840
given his admiration for Seath,

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.000
it seems that

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.720
he took on Seath's Soul aspects

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.620
Oceiros became this blind,

00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:58.900
mutated Pale Drake,

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:00.640
just like Seath, and

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:02.580
he was obsessed with this notion that

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:04.640
that he could use his royal blood

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:05.600
for a,

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:06.480
and I quote,

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:07.840
"greater purpose"

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:09.840
So, he fathered

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:11.680
this crossbreed child,

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:12.960
with his queen,

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:14.980
and named him Ocelote.

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:17.800
After giving birth to Ocelote,

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.380
her youngest child

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:22.320
the Queen of Lothric quietly disappeared.

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:24.560
Let's talk about the queen a little bit.

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:27.580
This queen either takes after Gwynevere

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:29.120
or is Gwynevere

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:30.620
because in Dark Souls I

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:33.860
Gwynevere left the ailing land of Lordran

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:37.320
in exactly the same manner that this queen

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.640
leaves the ailing land of Lothric.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.880
Also, Gwynevere of Dark Souls I

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:42.560
also

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.200
pushes the Chosen Undead to link the fire

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:46.980
and in Dark Souls III,

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:47.920
the Queen of Lothric

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.920
is obsessed with finding people

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:51.080
to link the fire,

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.000
even placing powerful rings

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.520
in the untended graves

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:55.820
in the hope

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:58.940
that one day, an Unkindled would rise to link the fire.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:02.540
So, the parallels between the two are undeniable

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:03.380
and

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:05.140
with the flame fading,

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:06.520
in Dark Souls III, and

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:08.100
this pus of man

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:10.040
spreading across the castle,

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:11.360
the Grand Archives

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:13.700
where Oceiros learned all of his knowledge

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:15.480
closed its doors for good,

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:17.460
and Oceiros remained,

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:19.520
walled off behind this garden

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:22.600
clutching his dragon crossbreed, Ocelote.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:24.000
Many assassins

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:26.320
were dispatched to his domain,

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:27.800
but none returned.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:28.680
We learn that

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:31.860
the Consumed King scribed his resilience

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.540
to the divine protection

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:34.760
of the dragonscale,

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:36.180
and when we stumble through

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:37.660
the Consumed Garden,

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.560
we find this Pale Drake

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:42.340
cradling his invisible infant crossbreed

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:43.720
before the fight.

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:45.920
He's a very vocal boss,

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:46.900
which is rare

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:48.920
and I think we need to disect

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.700
every line of his dialogue

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.860
"Ah, you ignorant slaves

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:59.060
finally taken notice have you...

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:04.100
...of the power of my beloved Ocelot,

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.300
Child of Dragons.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:09.560
Well,

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:12.080
I will not give him up.

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:15.120
for he is all that I have.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:18.100
So first of,

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:20.520
he calls us ignorant slaves

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:22.020
and I think this means that

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:22.980
he's arrogant

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:25.740
and he sees his subjects as slaves

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:26.480
or

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:27.440
perhaps

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.300
he's referring to us being slaves

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.480
to the linking of the Fire,

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.280
which Lothric is known for.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:33.600
Then he says,

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.680
"finally taken notice have you?"

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.700
which explains how he hasn't

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:38.620
been disturbed

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:40.020
for a very long time

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:41.340
He is out of the way;

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:42.780
he's not a main boss,

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:44.440
and he's also behind this

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:45.920
fair line of defense

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:48.320
within a locked off castle.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.020
We know it's been a long time

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:52.060
because the main boss we fight in this area

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:53.760
also gives us that impression.

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:56.360
Oceiros belives that this

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.840
crossbreed child named Ocelote

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:01.200
is worth taking notice of,

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:01.820
but

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:02.500
is he,

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:03.260
really?

00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:05.320
Ocelote is the crying baby

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:06.240
in the boss fight,

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:06.740
and

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:07.940
if we could see it,

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:08.960
we would probably see

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.000
that it's a crossbreed

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.980
between a Dragon and the Royal Bloodline,

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:14.940
and crossbreeds of this type

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:17.020
have existed in the past.

00:17:17.020 --> 00:17:18.500
Three others we know of

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:19.900
are the Emerald Herald,

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:21.060
Yorshka,

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.540
locked up in the tower,

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.220
and most notably,

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:24.940
Priscilla

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:26.420
from Dark Souls I

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:28.700
All that time ago, in Dark Souls I,

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:29.780
we theorized that

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:31.640
Priscilla was a crossbreed between

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:33.560
a Lord and a Dragon

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:35.480
specifically, a lot of people said that

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:37.980
she was the offspring of Seath the Scaleless

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:39.180
and Gwynevere,

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.140
and that parentage is

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:42.960
really strongly mirrored here

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:44.600
between Oceiros

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:45.720
and his Queen,

00:17:45.720 --> 00:17:47.160
who's basically Gwynevere,

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:49.420
and maybe I should've mentioned this earlier,

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:49.920
but

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.300
Priscilla also

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.460
had the ability to turn invisible,

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:55.260
which explains why Ocelote,

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.500
the baby he appears to be cradling,

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:58.800
cannot be seen,

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:01.740
and if Oceiros is blind like Seath was

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.480
then, perhaps he's

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:04.600
not even aware

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.160
that his child is invisble.

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:09.400
Priscilla also had this ability called Lifehunt,

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:10.860
which apparently,

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:12.260
the gods feared.

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:14.300
Presumably, Lifehunt

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:16.980
though it is never properly described,

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:18.200
can harm the Gods

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:18.700
and

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:20.380
maybe the threat of this

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:22.200
was what made the Queen of Lothric

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.380
leave her home

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:24.380
this time around.

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:26.560
Because it is easy to believe

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:29.360
that Oceiros would turn against his own kingdom,

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:32.100
after all, Seath's Soul Line,

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:33.200
as I'm calling it,

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:34.780
they've all been betrayers.

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:37.160
Seath betrayed the ancient dragons;

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:38.900
the Duke of the Writhing Ruins

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:40.520
in Dark Souls II set

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:42.520
spiders upon the townsfolk,

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:44.620
and I think it's most likely

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:46.220
that Oceiros hoped

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:47.880
that this crossbreed child

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:49.700
would be this powerful weapon

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:50.640
with Lifehunt,

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:53.500
based on how he talks about it during the fight

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:54.400
However,

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.480
this crossbreed didn't turn out

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:57.820
as Oceiros hoped,

00:18:57.820 --> 00:18:58.460
clearly,

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:00.520
and Oceiros' plan,

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:01.300
ehhh,

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:02.560
maybe not such a great one.

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:04.420
He is always referenced as

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:06.240
dilluded and mad

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:38.000
Originally,

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:40.180
Oceiros resembles a father

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:42.360
fighting to protect his child,

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.820
but as he nears death

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:46.460
he seems to become increasingly frustrated

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:49.120
with his crossbreed's lack of power

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:52.220
"Aaaaaaahhhhhh!

00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:57.820
Oceloooooooooooote!

00:19:58.280 --> 00:19:59.340
He appears even

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.340
to smash this baby

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:03.220
he was cradling upon the ground,

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:04.060
and

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:06.500
he reverts to a more feral stage

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.400
as he fights for his life

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:09.440
against us

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:10.740
The baby, however,

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:12.280
it continues to cry

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:13.880
even after this, so

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:15.780
yeah, mabye it's still alive.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:20.000
So, what are the consequenecs of Oceiros' treachery?

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:20.760
Well,

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:22.200
the collapse of his rule

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.100
was probably this fair part

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:25.660
of the collapse of the castle,

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:27.620
and even of Lothric Kingdom.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.240
Plus, the pus of man

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:31.820
is concentrated a lot in his garden,

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:33.580
but apart from that,

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:35.200
like the Nameless King,

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:36.440
I can't see

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:38.200
that his decisions had this

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.000
huge impact upon the world.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:42.140
In the previous video,

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:43.000
we talked about

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:46.000
how the Lothric bloodline resorted to

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.340
unspeakable means

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:49.320
to find a worthy heir

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:50.720
to link the fire.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.160
And my last thoughts

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:53.920
on this boss are that

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:56.440
perhaps Ocelote was created

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:59.180
with similar intents to Shanalotte

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:01.700
the dragon crossbreed of Dark Souls II that

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:03.620
men hoped would ward off

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:05.240
the Fire Linking Curse.

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.460
What's unclear

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:08.440
is whether Oceiros also

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:10.400
fathered Lorian and Lothric,

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:11.760
who are the two children of

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:13.880
the royal bloodline who refused

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.120
to link the fire.

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.780
Lorian, the eldest,

00:21:16.780 --> 00:21:18.160
he was raised as a knight,

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:20.140
and before his brother's curse

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:21.120
crippled him,

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:22.080
he was famed

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:23.940
for single-handedly slaying

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:25.200
the Demon Prince,

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:26.400
leaving his sword

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:28.700
eternally scorched with fire.

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:30.420
I'd wager that

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:31.880
this Demon Prince is

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:34.700
probably related to the Old Demon King,

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:36.180
if only because they're

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:37.980
the only hints of demon royalty

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:39.820
that we've ever seen in the game,

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:40.600
and if

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:42.560
these two are related, then

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:43.680
maybe the arena

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:46.300
that you fight the Old Demon King in

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:47.600
is also related.

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:50.880
There are piles of dead demon kin corpses,

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:52.900
which signifies that some battle

00:21:52.900 --> 00:21:54.060
took place here,

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:56.120
and of all these demons,

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:58.280
the shriveled Old Demon King

00:21:58.280 --> 00:22:00.260
is the only one to remain

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:02.100
now, like a clump of

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:03.220
burnt ash.

00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:05.220
He's the last living witness

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:06.760
of the Chaos of Izalith.

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:08.840
The Chaos Flame of Izalith

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:10.580
was born when the Witch of Izalith

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:12.660
attempted to use her own soul

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:14.020
to create another

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:15.100
First Flame

00:22:15.100 --> 00:22:15.960
Instead,

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:18.940
she turned ito this tumultuous Bed of Chaos,

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:21.400
which birthed demons from the fire

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:22.800
Beings that bore

00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:24.240
the smoldering essence of

00:22:24.240 --> 00:22:25.780
the Chaos Flame, and

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:28.080
were doomed, eventually, to perish.

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:29.820
The Old King's Hammer

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:30.920
has survived

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:32.320
since Old Izalith,

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:33.760
and is imbued

00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:35.820
with remnants of the Chaos Flame.

00:22:35.820 --> 00:22:37.680
We've talked about the Chaos Flame

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:39.360
so much over the years

00:22:39.360 --> 00:22:40.740
and in Dark Souls III,

00:22:40.740 --> 00:22:42.140
we definitely see

00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:44.600
when it and demon kind

00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:46.260
are at their lowest point.

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:47.520
Stray Demons,

00:22:47.520 --> 00:22:48.480
Capra Demons,

00:22:48.480 --> 00:22:49.760
Taurus Demons and

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:50.320
even

00:22:50.320 --> 00:22:51.820
hidden Centipede Demons,

00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:52.860
they're all dead

00:22:52.860 --> 00:22:54.460
in this arena, and

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:57.280
one Stray Demon we do face out in the world

00:22:57.280 --> 00:22:59.660
even lacks a trace of flame

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:01.340
showing how core

00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:03.220
this Flame is to their survival.

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:05.020
So, the demon race

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:06.100
and the Chaos Flame,

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:07.700
it's demonstratably

00:23:07.700 --> 00:23:08.960
at its lowest point

00:23:08.960 --> 00:23:09.900
in the series.

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:11.280
All of this said,

00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:14.100
demons are a largely undeveloped

00:23:14.100 --> 00:23:15.040
part of the lore,

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:17.680
I really do wish that they were designed to be

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:20.680
more than just brutish enemies, you know?

00:23:20.680 --> 00:23:22.660
With the Old Demon King, though,

00:23:22.660 --> 00:23:24.820
I liked it at the end of the fight,

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:26.460
you might not have noticed, but

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:27.700
if you keep him alive

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:29.160
at around ten percent health,

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:29.780
he

00:23:29.780 --> 00:23:31.700
in this desperate attempt

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:34.040
to fend us off with one final effort,

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:36.540
he releases all of his remaining energy.

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:37.560
He fails

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:39.200
and then he stays

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:40.600
panting on the ground

00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:41.680
indefinitely,

00:23:41.680 --> 00:23:43.500
unable even to lift

00:23:43.500 --> 00:23:44.660
his Great Hammer,

00:23:44.660 --> 00:23:47.520
surrounded by the corpses of his kind,

00:23:47.520 --> 00:23:49.100
and he's the last piece,

00:23:49.100 --> 00:23:50.060
of his race

00:23:50.060 --> 00:23:51.760
just reduced to

00:23:51.760 --> 00:23:53.660
flimsily batting us away

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:54.700
with one hand.

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:56.100
That kind of scene,

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:57.600
where there's no cut scene,

00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:59.380
there's no break in the gameplay

00:23:59.380 --> 00:24:01.200
and it still shows, you know,

00:24:01.200 --> 00:24:01.940
an emotion,

00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:03.700
a feeling that it wants to convey,

00:24:03.700 --> 00:24:05.360
that's good game design, and

00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:08.020
I feel like it's lost on a lot of people because

00:24:08.020 --> 00:24:09.180
most people will just

00:24:09.180 --> 00:24:10.280
finish this guy off

00:24:10.280 --> 00:24:12.260
in that last ten percent of his health, but

00:24:12.260 --> 00:24:13.620
it's a powerful scene.

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:14.980
And finally,

00:24:14.980 --> 00:24:16.560
the Cursed-Rotted Greatwood

00:24:16.560 --> 00:24:18.800
rooted in the Undead Settlement

00:24:18.800 --> 00:24:21.120
The Undead Settlement is a home to

00:24:21.120 --> 00:24:22.320
many Undead,

00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:24.060
and it's full of workers

00:24:24.060 --> 00:24:25.720
who are dedicated

00:24:25.720 --> 00:24:26.880
to the dissection

00:24:26.880 --> 00:24:28.360
and the burial of

00:24:28.360 --> 00:24:29.460
themeselves

00:24:29.460 --> 00:24:30.280
because

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:31.640
it makes sense that

00:24:31.640 --> 00:24:33.840
in this village and refuge

00:24:33.840 --> 00:24:36.020
full to the brim with Undead,

00:24:36.080 --> 00:24:37.520
that the primary task

00:24:37.520 --> 00:24:39.180
would end up being, you know,

00:24:39.180 --> 00:24:40.680
"What do we do

00:24:40.680 --> 00:24:42.040
with all the bodies that keep

00:24:42.040 --> 00:24:43.640
rising from the grave?".

00:24:43.640 --> 00:24:44.920
There's just this sheer

00:24:44.920 --> 00:24:46.840
problem of overpopulation,

00:24:46.840 --> 00:24:47.540
which

00:24:47.540 --> 00:24:49.120
could never be properly reduced

00:24:49.120 --> 00:24:49.680
because

00:24:49.680 --> 00:24:50.620
they never die,

00:24:50.620 --> 00:24:51.280
and

00:24:51.400 --> 00:24:52.200
as a result,

00:24:52.200 --> 00:24:53.140
in this place,

00:24:53.140 --> 00:24:55.580
you find Undead caged together

00:24:55.580 --> 00:24:57.580
dissected, hung, and buried,

00:24:57.580 --> 00:24:58.800
but probably

00:24:58.800 --> 00:25:01.420
just rising from the dead all the same

00:25:01.420 --> 00:25:03.740
to begin the process all over again

00:25:03.740 --> 00:25:04.740
Eventually,

00:25:04.740 --> 00:25:07.060
teachers from the Cathedral of the Deep

00:25:07.060 --> 00:25:08.540
came to take advantage

00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:09.880
of this climate

00:25:09.880 --> 00:25:11.440
in the Undead Settlement.

00:25:11.440 --> 00:25:12.840
The Evangelists,

00:25:12.840 --> 00:25:14.580
all women, came to

00:25:14.580 --> 00:25:17.340
enlighten inhabitants of the Undead Settlement

00:25:17.340 --> 00:25:18.900
and send carriers

00:25:18.900 --> 00:25:20.780
on the Path to Sacrifice,

00:25:20.800 --> 00:25:23.440
most likely to the Cathedral of the Deep,

00:25:23.440 --> 00:25:25.100
where they would be consumed

00:25:25.100 --> 00:25:26.580
by Aldrich as

00:25:26.580 --> 00:25:27.700
a sacrifice.

00:25:28.360 --> 00:25:28.960
So,

00:25:28.960 --> 00:25:31.800
it's no surprise really that

00:25:31.800 --> 00:25:34.300
all manners of curses managed to

00:25:34.360 --> 00:25:36.520
seep into the Undead Settlement

00:25:36.520 --> 00:25:37.240
for

00:25:37.240 --> 00:25:39.020
Undead were being dissected;

00:25:39.020 --> 00:25:41.440
their bones were being ground to dust,

00:25:41.440 --> 00:25:43.880
and they were buried within the earth.

00:25:44.320 --> 00:25:46.480
Rooted within that same soil,

00:25:46.480 --> 00:25:47.720
that same earth,

00:25:47.720 --> 00:25:49.160
was a Spirit Tree

00:25:49.160 --> 00:25:50.880
that would become known as

00:25:50.880 --> 00:25:52.600
the Curse-Rotted Greatwood

00:25:52.600 --> 00:25:54.820
Spirit Trees are another

00:25:54.820 --> 00:25:57.600
really undeveloped part of Souls Lore,

00:25:57.600 --> 00:25:59.420
and they appear mostly

00:25:59.420 --> 00:26:01.920
in item descriptions from Dark Souls II

00:26:02.120 --> 00:26:04.100
It's really easy to skip

00:26:04.100 --> 00:26:06.400
any description of a Spirit Tree.

00:26:06.580 --> 00:26:08.780
So, let's talk about what we know.

00:26:08.980 --> 00:26:10.900
They're descibed as magical,

00:26:10.900 --> 00:26:12.020
sentient,

00:26:12.020 --> 00:26:13.620
and supposedly,

00:26:13.620 --> 00:26:15.460
possessing divine powers.

00:26:15.620 --> 00:26:18.900
Two desciptions in particular reference them as

00:26:18.900 --> 00:26:21.040
appearing in a dream world

00:26:21.040 --> 00:26:22.640
related to Quella,

00:26:22.640 --> 00:26:24.140
who is the Goddess of Dream.

00:26:24.700 --> 00:26:25.900
There was this one

00:26:25.900 --> 00:26:28.480
talking Spirit Tree that also

00:26:28.480 --> 00:26:30.280
turned itself into a shield

00:26:30.280 --> 00:26:31.440
to protect

00:26:31.440 --> 00:26:33.580
a small, frightened child.

00:26:34.620 --> 00:26:36.020
I also have a hunch

00:26:36.020 --> 00:26:37.860
that this green tree

00:26:37.860 --> 00:26:40.480
that repairs items in Dark Souls II

00:26:40.480 --> 00:26:42.000
in the Sunken Kingdom,

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:43.300
I think it could be

00:26:43.300 --> 00:26:45.360
another type of Spirit Tree, as well,

00:26:45.360 --> 00:26:46.380
but again,

00:26:46.380 --> 00:26:48.260
this is just an educated guess.

00:26:48.260 --> 00:26:50.400
There's not much we know about this creatures.

00:26:50.880 --> 00:26:51.940
At any rate,

00:26:51.940 --> 00:26:54.720
the worst of the curses in the Undead Settlement

00:26:54.720 --> 00:26:55.900
were sealed away

00:26:55.900 --> 00:26:57.820
inside this Spirit Tree.

00:26:57.820 --> 00:26:59.760
Maybe it happened naturally,

00:26:59.760 --> 00:27:01.660
or maybe the townsfolk hoped

00:27:01.660 --> 00:27:02.780
that the tree would

00:27:02.780 --> 00:27:04.760
purify said curses, but

00:27:04.760 --> 00:27:06.540
eventually, however

00:27:06.540 --> 00:27:08.880
the curses took their toll and

00:27:08.880 --> 00:27:11.460
festered in the belly of the Greatwood.

00:27:11.760 --> 00:27:13.880
So, let's talk about what we find

00:27:13.880 --> 00:27:15.460
in the belly of the Greatwood.

00:27:15.700 --> 00:27:16.820
One thing we find

00:27:16.820 --> 00:27:18.600
is the Transposing Kiln,

00:27:18.600 --> 00:27:19.360
which is this

00:27:19.360 --> 00:27:21.000
artifact from Courland,

00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:23.480
stitched with Crystal Lizard hide.

00:27:23.660 --> 00:27:25.840
"Before I was a Lord of Cinder,

00:27:26.080 --> 00:27:27.500
I was a student

00:27:27.500 --> 00:27:29.160
of transposition,

00:27:29.380 --> 00:27:31.220
the process of extracting

00:27:31.220 --> 00:27:32.700
and coalescing

00:27:32.700 --> 00:27:34.980
the essence of a Soul.

00:27:35.740 --> 00:27:37.440
A forbidden art

00:27:37.620 --> 00:27:39.860
that once left a foul stain

00:27:39.860 --> 00:27:41.480
upon Courlund's honour.

00:27:42.600 --> 00:27:43.560
'Tis an art

00:27:43.560 --> 00:27:46.840
that grants powers once thought unattainable.

00:27:47.680 --> 00:27:50.020
Most Transposing Kilns

00:27:50.020 --> 00:27:51.700
were lost with Courlund,

00:27:52.020 --> 00:27:53.360
but this place

00:27:53.360 --> 00:27:55.560
is a crossing for all manner

00:27:55.560 --> 00:27:57.600
of cursed objects."

00:27:57.860 --> 00:27:58.820
Unwanted,

00:27:58.820 --> 00:28:01.160
cursed items were what were sealed

00:28:01.160 --> 00:28:02.180
within the Greatwood.

00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:02.780
So,

00:28:02.780 --> 00:28:04.120
it makes a degree of sense

00:28:04.120 --> 00:28:06.780
that the forbidden Transposing Kiln

00:28:06.780 --> 00:28:08.620
would also be sealed within it

00:28:08.620 --> 00:28:09.700
at some point.

00:28:09.700 --> 00:28:11.600
And with Ludleth's help,

00:28:11.600 --> 00:28:12.640
this kiln

00:28:12.640 --> 00:28:14.620
allows souls to be turned into a

00:28:14.620 --> 00:28:16.220
form we can use,

00:28:16.220 --> 00:28:17.840
like a weapon or a ring.

00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:19.520
These items reflect

00:28:19.520 --> 00:28:21.700
the souls that they were transposed from,

00:28:21.700 --> 00:28:23.600
and give us more insight

00:28:23.600 --> 00:28:24.860
into that being.

00:28:25.060 --> 00:28:26.180
Ludleth himself

00:28:26.180 --> 00:28:28.320
for example, drops the Skull Ring

00:28:28.320 --> 00:28:29.660
which was a wonder

00:28:29.660 --> 00:28:32.480
transposed from the soul of a Soul Feeder,

00:28:32.660 --> 00:28:35.780
a beast that insatiably absorbed souls.

00:28:35.780 --> 00:28:37.560
to feed its own power

00:28:37.920 --> 00:28:41.540
So, when we transpose the Cursed-Rotted Greatwood's Soul

00:28:41.540 --> 00:28:44.280
we aren't getting items related to the Greatwood.

00:28:44.280 --> 00:28:46.220
We're kind of getting items that were

00:28:46.220 --> 00:28:48.980
related to the curses that were within

00:28:48.980 --> 00:28:49.960
the Greatwood.

00:28:49.960 --> 00:28:51.000
For example,

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:53.300
one is the Spear of Arstor

00:28:53.300 --> 00:28:55.660
who was this knight from Carim,

00:28:55.660 --> 00:28:57.960
fond of impaling his enemies,

00:28:57.960 --> 00:28:59.760
and he was credited with

00:28:59.760 --> 00:29:01.380
the dreadful creation of the

00:29:01.380 --> 00:29:02.860
Bite Set of rings.

00:29:02.860 --> 00:29:03.900
This is one thing

00:29:03.900 --> 00:29:05.620
that we get from within the Greatwood.

00:29:05.620 --> 00:29:08.280
Another is the Hollowslayer Greatsword,

00:29:08.280 --> 00:29:10.000
which harbors the fears that

00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:12.500
lurk within the minds of Hollows,

00:29:12.500 --> 00:29:14.060
and is more effective

00:29:14.060 --> 00:29:15.060
at killing them.

00:29:15.060 --> 00:29:15.700
So,

00:29:15.700 --> 00:29:16.880
this sword, it's

00:29:16.880 --> 00:29:18.540
very well known in Souls.

00:29:18.540 --> 00:29:20.020
It once belonged to

00:29:20.020 --> 00:29:22.320
Lucatile of Dark Souls II, and

00:29:22.320 --> 00:29:24.080
you might be able to see why

00:29:24.080 --> 00:29:26.280
the Hollows of the Undead Settlement would

00:29:26.280 --> 00:29:27.940
seal this sword away.

00:29:27.940 --> 00:29:30.360
It was known for killing their kind, and

00:29:30.360 --> 00:29:32.000
that's one hell of a curse

00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:32.780
for them.

00:29:34.800 --> 00:29:36.300
Let's talk about some comments from

00:29:36.300 --> 00:29:37.280
the previous video

00:29:37.280 --> 00:29:38.940
before I end this video

00:29:38.940 --> 00:29:41.120
SiestaYonJyuGo says,

00:29:47.200 --> 00:29:47.700
So,

00:29:47.700 --> 00:29:49.580
Siesta is referring to the fact that

00:29:49.580 --> 00:29:53.040
Aldrich can cast a version of Lifehunt Scythe,

00:29:53.220 --> 00:29:54.580
and Lifehunt Scythe

00:29:54.580 --> 00:29:55.820
was a spell that

00:29:55.820 --> 00:29:58.260
Priscilla could use and he's wondering why

00:29:58.260 --> 00:30:00.640
I think that Aldrich saw Yorshka,

00:30:01.160 --> 00:30:02.360
and he's right,

00:30:02.360 --> 00:30:04.280
Priscilla might make more sense

00:30:04.280 --> 00:30:05.320
in retrospect,

00:30:05.320 --> 00:30:06.960
but my thinking is

00:30:06.960 --> 00:30:08.520
base around my theory

00:30:08.520 --> 00:30:10.160
of a lot of the characters in the game.

00:30:10.740 --> 00:30:11.520
You know how earlier

00:30:11.520 --> 00:30:13.100
we were talking about Oceiros

00:30:13.100 --> 00:30:15.140
and how he takes after Seath.

00:30:15.380 --> 00:30:16.020
Well,

00:30:16.020 --> 00:30:17.520
in my perspective,

00:30:18.120 --> 00:30:20.680
Oceiros pretty much represents Seath

00:30:20.680 --> 00:30:21.560
in this game,

00:30:21.560 --> 00:30:23.400
and in a same sort of manner,

00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:26.120
Yorshka, to me, represents Priscilla,

00:30:26.120 --> 00:30:28.540
uh, and that goes a bit more deeper than just

00:30:28.540 --> 00:30:29.700
being a descendant.

00:30:29.700 --> 00:30:31.260
I think that she

00:30:31.260 --> 00:30:32.620
fits the same role

00:30:32.620 --> 00:30:33.940
in this timeline

00:30:33.940 --> 00:30:36.140
as Priscilla did in her timeline

00:30:36.140 --> 00:30:37.640
Priscilla was a crossbreed

00:30:37.640 --> 00:30:38.980
locked away in a painting

00:30:38.980 --> 00:30:40.260
near Anor Londo,

00:30:40.260 --> 00:30:41.040
and

00:30:41.040 --> 00:30:43.420
Yorshka is also a crossbreed

00:30:43.420 --> 00:30:44.940
locked away in a tower,

00:30:44.940 --> 00:30:46.440
near Anor Londo.

00:30:46.760 --> 00:30:48.100
Both of them were

00:30:48.100 --> 00:30:50.620
probably locked away for being crossbreeds, and

00:30:50.620 --> 00:30:53.460
yeah, so when I say he dreamt of Yorshka,

00:30:53.460 --> 00:30:55.480
I assumed that Yorshka would have

00:30:55.480 --> 00:30:57.780
the same Lifehunt Scythe skill,

00:30:57.780 --> 00:30:59.800
and Yorshka inhabits this world,

00:30:59.800 --> 00:31:02.080
whereas Priscilla hasn't been proved.

